{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-7793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+8\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+16y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda +4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-4$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9409bd4a3346aa8184acab633923a01a38021d9f85994e0a271f3dc52700c1e6"} {"question" "q-7793" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7793" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{2x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{2x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7793" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{25y}{4}=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{25}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +\\frac{25}{4}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +\\frac{25}{4}=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2})(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9409bd4a3346aa8184acab633923a01a38021d9f85994e0a271f3dc52700c1e6"} {"question" "q-7796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{3x/2}+Bx{e}^{3x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{-5x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{5x/2}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{x/2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-7796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-14\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+49y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-14\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+49{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +49) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +49=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -7) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -7)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =7$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{7x}+Bx{e}^{7x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9409bd4a3346aa8184acab633923a01a38021d9f85994e0a271f3dc52700c1e6"} {"question" "q-90958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-7x}+Bx{e}^{-7x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-7x}+B{e}^{2x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{14x}+Bx{e}^{14x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{7x}+Bx{e}^{7x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{7x}+B{e}^{-7x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{7x}+Bx{e}^{7x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+\\frac{9}{4}y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-3x/2}$ and $x{e}^{-3x/2}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $x{e}^{-3x/2}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x/2}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9409bd4a3346aa8184acab633923a01a38021d9f85994e0a271f3dc52700c1e6"} {"question" "q-90964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x{e}^{-3x/2}"] ["math" "3{e}^{-3x/2}+x{e}^{-3x/2}"] ["math" "8{e}^{-3x/2}-3x{e}^{-3x/2}"] ["math" "x{e}^{-3x/2}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x/2}"] ["math" "{e}^{-3x/2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x{e}^{-3x/2}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x/2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-16{y}^{′}+64y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-16\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+64{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-16\\lambda +64) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-16\\lambda +64 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\lambda -8)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =8$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{8x}$ and $x{e}^{8x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${x}^{2}{e}^{8x}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9409bd4a3346aa8184acab633923a01a38021d9f85994e0a271f3dc52700c1e6"} {"question" "q-90966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x{e}^{8x}"] ["math" "3{e}^{8x}+2x{e}^{8x}"] ["math" "{e}^{8x}"] ["math" "{e}^{8x}-x{e}^{8x}"] ["math" "{x}^{2}{e}^{8x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229bb9ae43d419b5df52a9acf281c11ae005e867b"} {"question" "q-90966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}{e}^{8x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073904/state.json" "file_sha256" "85c5f235276b5f301d40d74229